      "Pakistan operates a federal system in which the taxation of goods and services is split between the federal government and the provinces. While the Federal Board of Revenue collects sales tax on goods under federal law, sales tax on services falls under the jurisdiction of the provinces following the eighteenth constitutional amendment. Each province has established its own revenue authority to collect this tax, and businesses that provide services must understand which authority applies to them based on where the service is rendered or consumed.",
      "The Punjab Revenue Authority, commonly known as PRA, administers sales tax on services in Punjab. It covers a broad range of services including telecommunications, advertising, franchise services, construction, consultancy, and many professional services. Businesses providing taxable services within Punjab must register with PRA, charge sales tax on their invoices at the applicable rate, and file monthly returns detailing their output tax collected and any input tax adjustments they are entitled to claim.",
      "The Sindh Revenue Board, known as SRB, performs a similar function in Sindh and was in fact the first provincial authority established after the constitutional changes. SRB has its own list of taxable services, its own registration process, and its own e-portal for filing returns. Businesses operating in Karachi and other parts of Sindh that provide services such as banking, insurance, courier, restaurants, and various professional services generally need to register with SRB rather than the federal board.",
      "The Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Revenue Authority, or KPRA, handles services taxation in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa. Its scope and rates may differ from PRA and SRB, and it maintains its own schedule of taxable services along with specific exemptions relevant to the province. Balochistan similarly has its own revenue authority for services, so a business operating across multiple provinces may need to register with more than one authority depending on where it delivers services.",
