      "The rapid growth of online marketplaces and social media selling in Pakistan has created a large and diverse community of e-commerce sellers, ranging from individuals running small home-based shops on social media to larger businesses operating through their own websites and established online marketplaces. Regardless of scale, anyone earning income through e-commerce activities in Pakistan is generally subject to the same fundamental tax obligations that apply to any other business, and treating online selling as somehow outside the tax net is a common but risky misconception.",
